+# Live — the running Dictate system, as real objects
+
+What it is, shown at [`/framework/ux/Dictate/live/`](/framework/ux/Dictate/live/): one
+nested tree, `Dictate` at the root, its mic(s), the one shared `Floor`, and every open
+chat session underneath — each row a real, live object (`inspect()`,
+[`ux/Content/Object`](/framework/ux/Content/Object/)), not a diagram of one. Beside the
+tree on a wide screen (below it once the screen is too narrow to hold both), the same
+three classes as class cards — same icon, every property NAME a fresh instance will
+have, every method it answers to.
+
+## Use
+
+A class joins the tree with one line, the same opt-in `core/track/track.js` already
+offers every class on the site:
+
+```js
+import { track } from "/framework/core/track/track.js";
+track(MyClass);                       // once, at module scope
+class MyClass { constructor(){ MyClass.track(this); } }
+MyClass.instances()                   // → every live one, read by live/page.js's redraw()
+```
+
+`Klass.weights = { properties: "a b c" }` (a plain static, read by `inspect()`'s own
+`properties:` option) decides which properties show, and in what order — the simplest
+form of "a weight decides the order."
+
+## Watch out
+
+- Rebuilt every second (`setInterval`, stopped on unmount via the same `MutationObserver`
+  trick `../page.js`'s own `demo_mount()` uses) — a row you opened stays open (a `WeakMap`
+  key per live object plus a captured `toggle` listener, `redraw()`'s own `open_keys`), but
+  everything inside it still repaints from the real object's current values each tick.
+- Only `Dictate`, `Floor` (`../Floor.js`) and `ChatController` (`../ChatController.js`)
+  opted in — most classes never call `track()`, and show up nowhere here on purpose.
+- Six mic rows all read `#1 idle … #6 idle` with no word for which SURFACE each one is
+  mounted on (the ✦ sheet, the drawer, this page's own demo) — a real gap, left open: no
+  `Dictate`/`ComposerMic` instance carries that today, and giving every one of the half
+  dozen call sites a new `surface:` label is a change this task's fence doesn't reach.
+- **A seventh tab (LIVE) still wraps to two rows at 400** (round 4 shortened `demo/page.js`'s
+  own tab title, "Send modes" → "Modes", which was enough to fit all seven at 1200 and up —
+  but not at 400, where every tab label is naturally tighter). The real fix is `ext/tabs`'
+  own overflow story (today: scroll only, no grouping, no "more ▾" — `ext/tabs/readme.md`'s
+  "Watch out"), a site-wide component this task's fence doesn't reach. Left as a named
+  trade-off, not silently dropped.
+
+## More
+
+- [`doc/status-signals.md`](/framework/ux/Dictate/doc/status-signals/) — the status words
+  this same trio's `Dictate` instance earns, and the one real event behind each
+- [`../readme.md`](/framework/ux/Dictate/) — Dictate itself
